{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788032074015965001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"bouncy-peacockish-titmouse","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"fc30f3679748e03c58dfa04173ddac21080571dbd9e1253d914c56b2a35b6a86","event_uuid":"63cb9ce7-113b-4410-a805-1ed4155cb7d8","position":{"commit_sha":"0891542fe6119d0562cf319af19c199a5acd30e5","position":"1788029128934029385-63cb9ce7-113b-4410-a805-1ed4155cb7d8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"c364bc754a368c70f0069a0fbe8bbc59419c12c4b46842be9cb18b319699088f","event_uuid":"56aa875d-2ccd-4c78-8e5c-5e06fa65f12c","position":{"commit_sha":"41f0ecda15c201471300dfe20e2a26c13f02a562","position":"1788029248387610821-56aa875d-2ccd-4c78-8e5c-5e06fa65f12c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"59a9dc023998a46d6cc9462a8e7d6ced9545a519bc0a26d0f565ef2020d91ea6","event_uuid":"d4bf512c-cbd0-494c-b5e9-6d87076e1806","position":{"commit_sha":"751a4ef60a1730d765bf8347e94ae8dc63e07f2a","position":"1788029589131565401-d4bf512c-cbd0-494c-b5e9-6d87076e1806"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788029128934029385,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"56aa875d-2ccd-4c78-8e5c-5e06fa65f12c","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"4bd8-a2bb-813b-427e"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nPass 3 (`src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/decide.py`: `validity()`, `impact_plan()`, `pass3_decide`, `DEFAULT_BLOCK_THRESHOLD`, per-criterion `block_threshold`/`default_posture` in `criteria_routing.json`, the execution-phase raise in `orchestrator.py`, `DEFAULT_ADVISORY_CAP`) is deterministic and every input it needs — the Pass-2 `verification` vector, `block_threshold`, `blocking_enabled`, `review_phase` — is in the v2 sidecar. `docs/calibration/plan_v5_rescore.py` and `docs/experiments/calibrate_plan_review_thresholds.py` prove the replay works but are one-off scripts with hardcoded baselines. Any proposal touching Pass-3 logic or thresholds should be assessable over all ~4,300 reviews for free.\n\n## Approach\n\nBuild `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier0.py`:\n\n- Input: the corpus + labels, and a **candidate** = a Python callable/module path for the decide function, a routing overlay JSON (thresholds/postures), and `[verify]` config overrides. Default candidate = current code, so \"replay current code\" is the identity check.\n- Run `orchestrator.pass3_over_findings` (or `pass3_decide` per finding) for baseline and candidate over every review; keep the stored decision as the historical reference too.\n- Report (`tier0-<candidate-name>-<date>.md` + JSON): verdict flip matrix (PASS/BLOCK/INDETERMINATE), friction rate (share of reviews BLOCKed), per-criterion block/advisory/drop deltas, priority distribution shift, and label-proxy metrics — block rate on `escaped_defect`/`completion_failed_after_pass` tickets (recall proxy) vs block rate on `clean_close` tickets (false-positive proxy), and share of blocking findings that were `resolved_by_author`. Every delta is annotated against the noise band from the labels ticket.\n- Post-verdict floors (novelty/completion/drift) are replayed only when their inputs are present in the sidecar (`coverage.drift`, prior findings); otherwise reported as not replayed.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier0.py`, `report.py` (new)\n- `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/tier0-*.md` (generated)\n- `tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_tier0.py` (new)\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit: identity replay of a fixture corpus yields zero diffs; a candidate overlay lowering one criterion's threshold flips exactly the fixture findings whose priority sits between old and new thresholds; a v1 sidecar lacking `block_threshold` is skipped and counted. E2E (manual, recorded in the report): replay the documented plan-v4→plan-v5 impact-model change and reproduce the effect recorded in `docs/calibration/`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `python -m rebar.llm.evals.plan_replay tier0 --candidate current` over the real corpus reports zero verdict flips against stored decisions for reviews whose `impact_model_version` matches current; checked by the generated report.\n- [ ] Replaying the plan-v4→plan-v5 change reproduces its documented direction and approximate magnitude; checked against `docs/calibration/`.\n- [ ] The report contains verdict flip matrix, friction rate, per-criterion deltas and the label-proxy recall/false-positive metrics, each annotated relative to the noise band; checked by inspection of one report.\n- [ ] A full-corpus run completes in under 5 minutes on a laptop with zero LLM calls; checked by timing and by running without provider credentials.\n- [ ] Unit tests pass in `make test`.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier0.py","reason":"Pass-3 replay"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/report.py","reason":"diff report"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/__main__.py","reason":"module entry point"},{"path":"docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/","reason":"generated reports"},{"path":"tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_tier0.py","reason":"unit tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","4bd8-a2bb-813b-427e"],["parent","759e-7dc1-675c-4877"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"759e-7dc1-675c-4877","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["plan-review","evals","tier-0","pass-3"],"ticket_id":"5d19-52e0-7c26-47fb","ticket_type":"story","title":"Tier-0 harness: replay Pass-3 calculation, thresholds and routing overlays over the whole corpus (zero LLM)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["63cb9ce7-113b-4410-a805-1ed4155cb7d8","56aa875d-2ccd-4c78-8e5c-5e06fa65f12c","d4bf512c-cbd0-494c-b5e9-6d87076e1806"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788032074015965001,"uuid":"ace7d15d-9f28-413e-b48e-31559265dde0"}